1
00:00:00,005 --> 00:00:01,500
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,503 --> 00:00:03,018
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:03,618 --> 00:00:04,727
(Episode 47)

4
00:00:04,818 --> 00:00:05,818
Really?

5
00:00:05,820 --> 00:00:08,358
Yeah, Do Do Hee's completely nuts.

6
00:00:08,378 --> 00:00:10,465
She blew off the shoot yesterday.

7
00:00:11,298 --> 00:00:13,618
Shooting got pushed back
because of her. So annoying.

8
00:00:14,265 --> 00:00:15,526
Can she really do that?

9
00:00:15,892 --> 00:00:19,332
Delaying the shoot must cost the company
money, right?

10
00:00:19,424 --> 00:00:21,995
She'll probably just
buy her way out of it.

11
00:00:22,545 --> 00:00:25,318
Your brother is so nice that
he might just make her pay a fine.

12
00:00:25,631 --> 00:00:27,371
I hope he makes her pay a huge one.

13
00:00:27,852 --> 00:00:29,598
Don't call him "my brother."
You'll get us in trouble.

14
00:00:30,071 --> 00:00:31,634
Be formal. Call him Director.

15
00:00:31,715 --> 00:00:32,945
Okay.

16
00:00:33,672 --> 00:00:35,738
Why did I call him that?

17
00:00:36,832 --> 00:00:38,461
I guess I just want to have a brother
like him.

18
00:00:39,989 --> 00:00:41,165
I'm not stopping you.

19
00:00:41,412 --> 00:00:43,405
But because of me,
you absolutely can't call him...

20
00:00:43,407 --> 00:00:44,460
Got it!

21
00:00:46,298 --> 00:00:48,278
After all that,
you're buying him a gift for the shoot?

22
00:00:52,705 --> 00:00:53,705
Look.

23
00:00:55,450 --> 00:00:56,450
Pretty, right?

24
00:00:56,745 --> 00:00:59,385
I was invited,
so I can't exactly show up empty-handed.

25
00:01:02,365 --> 00:01:04,265
- Hey, Jung A.
- Hello.

26
00:01:06,365 --> 00:01:08,645
Let's see, how did I do this again?

27
00:01:09,872 --> 00:01:11,218
Mom, are you going back
to the Oriental Medicine Clinic?

28
00:01:13,452 --> 00:01:16,238
I won't misunderstand you,
so don't misunderstand me either.

29
00:01:16,312 --> 00:01:17,954
I'm just a patient.

30
00:01:19,275 --> 00:01:20,898
What are you doing?
The order's already in.

31
00:01:20,931 --> 00:01:22,077
Hurry up and make it.

32
00:01:26,257 --> 00:01:27,510
How's the shoot going?

33
00:01:27,839 --> 00:01:29,858
It's fun. It's a whole different world.

34
00:01:30,412 --> 00:01:32,136
I can't wait to see it.

35
00:01:32,417 --> 00:01:33,417
By the way,

36
00:01:33,658 --> 00:01:34,752
if you need clothes, come by.

37
00:01:34,812 --> 00:01:37,556
I'll see if I can get
a couple of outfits sponsored for you.

38
00:01:38,124 --> 00:01:39,124
Really?

39
00:01:39,595 --> 00:01:40,668
Ma'am, you're the best!

40
00:01:43,712 --> 00:01:45,864
Your drinks are ready.

41
00:01:46,479 --> 00:01:48,556
Okay, got it.

42
00:01:49,018 --> 00:01:50,665
Thank you.

43
00:01:50,852 --> 00:01:52,617
- Have a good day.
- Thanks.

44
00:01:55,340 --> 00:01:56,914
This is amazing.

45
00:01:57,594 --> 00:01:58,604
What's with you?

46
00:01:58,684 --> 00:02:00,549
She's going to sponsor my outfits.

47
00:02:00,552 --> 00:02:02,705
I was worried
I'd have to buy everything myself.

48
00:02:04,932 --> 00:02:06,132
What are you talking about?

49
00:02:06,898 --> 00:02:08,498
Why would my mom sponsor anything?

50
00:02:10,503 --> 00:02:11,680
- How?
- What?

51
00:02:12,834 --> 00:02:14,031
About that...

52
00:02:17,785 --> 00:02:20,038
So that's why you decided to get married?

53
00:02:21,879 --> 00:02:24,411
Who decides to get married
over something like that?

54
00:02:24,413 --> 00:02:26,163
You two are really something.

55
00:02:27,072 --> 00:02:28,072
Are we?

56
00:02:28,685 --> 00:02:29,916
But it really broke my heart...

57
00:02:30,877 --> 00:02:32,435
when she talked about how lonely...

58
00:02:32,802 --> 00:02:35,217
she'd been in that house all this time.

59
00:02:35,245 --> 00:02:37,578
Then she should've married
a long time ago.

60
00:02:37,878 --> 00:02:39,813
Why wait until now
after clinging to that life?

61
00:02:39,943 --> 00:02:41,096
It's ridiculous.

62
00:02:41,098 --> 00:02:43,678
Still, I'm so glad she made up her mind.

63
00:02:43,838 --> 00:02:47,168
Yeong Ju was so adamant
that I thought I'd have to give up.

64
00:02:47,982 --> 00:02:49,023
I'm so happy.

65
00:02:49,304 --> 00:02:50,358
Please congratulate us.

66
00:02:52,272 --> 00:02:54,488
- What about me, Sa Bin?
- What?

67
00:02:55,972 --> 00:02:58,005
Don't worry.

68
00:02:58,198 --> 00:03:00,525
You're my friend forever.

69
00:03:00,978 --> 00:03:04,350
Yeong Ju doesn't doubt.
She's such an angel.

70
00:03:10,663 --> 00:03:11,743
Sa Bin.

71
00:03:17,312 --> 00:03:20,005
Look at her. Look at those eyes.

72
00:03:21,425 --> 00:03:23,798
I'm a patient, you know?

73
00:03:24,253 --> 00:03:25,805
I'm a patient here.

74
00:03:26,252 --> 00:03:28,032
Can't you go to another clinic?

75
00:03:28,565 --> 00:03:30,830
Watching you two together
makes me uncomfortable.

76
00:03:30,832 --> 00:03:32,398
Honestly, this brings back bad memories.

77
00:03:32,432 --> 00:03:34,451
Maestro is here because she's sick.

78
00:03:35,285 --> 00:03:36,824
Did you come to see me?

79
00:03:38,179 --> 00:03:40,711
What? What's this? A lunchbox?

80
00:03:41,485 --> 00:03:43,038
I made some dried pollock porridge.

81
00:03:43,046 --> 00:03:44,913
You were pretty sick yesterday.
Are you feeling better?

82
00:03:45,823 --> 00:03:46,878
Blow on my owie.

83
00:03:49,005 --> 00:03:51,565
Sa Bin, what are you doing?
You were taking my pulse.

84
00:03:56,038 --> 00:03:57,598
Sa Bin doesn't like porridge.

85
00:03:57,692 --> 00:03:59,524
Neither of us eats porridge.

86
00:03:59,677 --> 00:04:00,965
Maestro.

87
00:04:02,411 --> 00:04:03,411
Seriously.

88
00:04:04,958 --> 00:04:07,358
You really don't like porridge?

89
00:04:07,392 --> 00:04:08,538
My dear Yeong Ju,

90
00:04:09,192 --> 00:04:10,511
why is your jealousy so cute?

91
00:04:12,638 --> 00:04:14,791
I love porridge now. I'll eat it all.

92
00:04:15,665 --> 00:04:17,785
I'll eat every last grain myself.

93
00:04:20,312 --> 00:04:21,312
Look at you.

94
00:04:21,892 --> 00:04:24,612
You're still breaking out in a cold sweat.

95
00:04:26,678 --> 00:04:27,678
Wait.

96
00:04:29,780 --> 00:04:31,257
So this is what it's like.

97
00:04:31,478 --> 00:04:32,992
Having someone who's yours.

98
00:04:38,491 --> 00:04:39,706
Doctor, your patients...

99
00:04:40,887 --> 00:04:42,031
Your patients...

100
00:04:43,955 --> 00:04:46,952
I'll get going. Go ahead and work.

101
00:04:47,985 --> 00:04:49,058
Wait a second.

102
00:04:49,991 --> 00:04:52,331
I'll call you
after I'm done seeing patients.

103
00:04:52,392 --> 00:04:53,771
We have to go see our house.

104
00:04:54,645 --> 00:04:55,645
"Our house?"

105
00:05:04,895 --> 00:05:06,148
Seriously.

106
00:05:13,878 --> 00:05:14,878
Yes, Director.

107
00:05:15,245 --> 00:05:16,338
You went to the hospital, right?

108
00:05:16,732 --> 00:05:17,778
How's your face?

109
00:05:18,045 --> 00:05:19,227
They want to see me in three days.

110
00:05:19,728 --> 00:05:21,852
That's good. Take care of yourself.

111
00:05:22,096 --> 00:05:23,105
Don't hang up.

112
00:05:23,605 --> 00:05:25,036
Aren't you coming today?

113
00:05:25,975 --> 00:05:27,292
Please come visit me.

114
00:05:27,552 --> 00:05:29,212
Tell your boyfriend to come.

115
00:05:29,678 --> 00:05:31,780
Get well soon, and we'll talk then.

116
00:05:31,928 --> 00:05:33,423
Director, please come.

117
00:05:34,184 --> 00:05:35,184
Will you?

118
00:05:35,468 --> 00:05:37,165
I'm bored, and I can't even go out.

119
00:05:37,592 --> 00:05:39,150
I'll treat you to something good.

120
00:05:39,698 --> 00:05:40,698
Please.

121
00:05:42,639 --> 00:05:43,831
Got it.

122
00:06:05,285 --> 00:06:06,289
The CEO?

123
00:06:07,057 --> 00:06:08,057
Yeah.

124
00:06:08,392 --> 00:06:11,550
I heard Mr. Song was going to
partner with someone, but it fell through.

125
00:06:11,658 --> 00:06:14,863
He had a deal with Mr. Shin,
but Mr. Shin backed out. He's on his own.

126
00:06:14,865 --> 00:06:18,038
So take over as CEO
and run your dad's company.

127
00:06:18,618 --> 00:06:21,600
See how loyal I am?
I wonder if your mom knows.

128
00:06:21,602 --> 00:06:23,365
No. I'm not doing it.

129
00:06:23,478 --> 00:06:25,478
I can't stand that man.

130
00:06:25,999 --> 00:06:28,705
Watch your mouth, you brat.

131
00:06:30,591 --> 00:06:33,670
Why did your mom wait so long to remarry?

132
00:06:33,672 --> 00:06:36,491
What are you talking about?
What does that have to do with this?

133
00:06:36,493 --> 00:06:38,478
I wish she'd done it sooner.

134
00:06:39,332 --> 00:06:42,405
I was going to take your dad to Europe.

135
00:06:42,612 --> 00:06:44,025
He said he'd go too.

136
00:06:44,611 --> 00:06:48,145
But once we got to Europe,
there'd be nothing he could do.

137
00:06:48,858 --> 00:06:50,465
So I gave up.

138
00:06:50,592 --> 00:06:54,558
We ended up hiding Ji Ni
and making her miserable.

139
00:06:55,545 --> 00:06:58,191
Why are you telling me all this?

140
00:06:58,745 --> 00:07:01,058
That's how this company came to be.

141
00:07:01,425 --> 00:07:05,150
Your dad started this company for you
after you lost your leg in an accident.

142
00:07:06,152 --> 00:07:07,923
He said it was entirely his.

143
00:07:07,925 --> 00:07:09,536
What do you think that meant?

144
00:07:09,991 --> 00:07:11,052
You.

145
00:07:12,012 --> 00:07:15,934
You were the only person
he wanted to apologize to until the end.

146
00:07:18,292 --> 00:07:19,572
This is driving me crazy.

147
00:07:20,425 --> 00:07:21,878
It's driving me crazy too.

148
00:07:22,052 --> 00:07:25,976
Your mom locked us in this cycle,
and now she's getting to walk away.

149
00:07:27,222 --> 00:07:29,680
- You shouldn't say that.
- Okay.

150
00:07:29,975 --> 00:07:31,303
You lose your temper so easily.

151
00:07:31,664 --> 00:07:33,082
Anyway,

152
00:07:33,318 --> 00:07:36,125
I don't want to talk about
that clueless woman anymore.

153
00:07:36,550 --> 00:07:38,305
So save this company.

154
00:07:39,505 --> 00:07:42,271
Honestly, I didn't want
to keep that promise,

155
00:07:42,452 --> 00:07:45,205
so I tried to take full control
and run it myself, but that failed.

156
00:07:45,878 --> 00:07:48,298
But I can't let someone else have it.

157
00:07:49,338 --> 00:07:51,700
Once I find Attorney Byeon,

158
00:07:51,794 --> 00:07:53,752
I'll get back all the money
they took from me.

159
00:07:55,218 --> 00:07:57,518
Being broke makes me look awful.
I can't live like this.

160
00:07:58,418 --> 00:08:02,112
Your grandpa didn't even buy Ji Ni
a gold ring for her first birthday...

161
00:08:06,411 --> 00:08:08,629
Don't be stubborn. Think it over.

162
00:08:09,077 --> 00:08:10,077
I'm leaving.

163
00:08:15,480 --> 00:08:16,685
Loyal? What a joke.

164
00:08:20,791 --> 00:08:22,478
Where on earth is Seung Hyun?

165
00:08:22,705 --> 00:08:23,951
Come back already.

166
00:08:24,385 --> 00:08:25,698
This is driving me crazy.

167
00:08:49,512 --> 00:08:50,645
Who is it?

168
00:09:14,470 --> 00:09:15,537
Get me some water.

169
00:09:20,871 --> 00:09:22,212
You're just going to drink it, right?

170
00:09:22,731 --> 00:09:23,802
You won't throw it on me, right?

171
00:09:25,540 --> 00:09:27,398
What are you, a plant?
Why would I water you?

172
00:09:35,012 --> 00:09:36,670
Why did you suddenly change your mind?

173
00:09:36,672 --> 00:09:38,511
I never expected much,

174
00:09:38,514 --> 00:09:41,391
but I didn't think you'd flip so quickly.

175
00:09:41,444 --> 00:09:43,118
Neither did I, but...

176
00:09:43,905 --> 00:09:44,960
it just happened.

177
00:09:45,042 --> 00:09:46,043
But why?

178
00:09:46,264 --> 00:09:47,445
I just want to know why.

179
00:09:49,372 --> 00:09:52,598
If you were younger, I'd ask
if you were pregnant.

180
00:09:53,591 --> 00:09:55,898
But at your age, it's too awkward to ask.

181
00:09:55,925 --> 00:09:57,605
This is a private matter between us.

182
00:09:58,012 --> 00:09:59,592
Don't ask any more questions.

183
00:10:00,293 --> 00:10:02,668
- Don't talk to me like we're equals.
- We're both from the 36th class.

184
00:10:02,670 --> 00:10:03,697
So what's the problem?

185
00:10:03,965 --> 00:10:05,311
I saw my yearbook.

186
00:10:06,025 --> 00:10:07,118
Do you seriously...

187
00:10:07,339 --> 00:10:10,139
want to marry into this family
and have me boss you around?

188
00:10:10,167 --> 00:10:11,405
Is that what you want?

189
00:10:11,465 --> 00:10:14,414
Sa Bin isn't a child,
and we'll live separately anyway.

190
00:10:14,609 --> 00:10:15,725
Just give up.

191
00:10:15,758 --> 00:10:17,352
You can't break us up.

192
00:10:17,945 --> 00:10:20,091
Please tell your husband too.

193
00:10:20,178 --> 00:10:22,988
Tell him we'll do our best
to live a good life together.

194
00:10:23,902 --> 00:10:26,146
- I'm counting on you, Sun Kyung.
- Hey!

195
00:10:26,933 --> 00:10:28,200
I can't believe you.

196
00:10:30,705 --> 00:10:34,777
If you have any decency,

197
00:10:34,779 --> 00:10:38,197
how can you take advantage of a pushover?

198
00:10:39,544 --> 00:10:43,131
Stop it. You're his sister-in-law,
so why act like you're his wife?

199
00:10:43,392 --> 00:10:44,958
Sa Bin and I aren't having an affair,

200
00:10:44,960 --> 00:10:46,502
and we're not hurting anyone.

201
00:10:46,609 --> 00:10:49,133
So why are you behaving like this?

202
00:10:49,934 --> 00:10:50,962
How dare you!

203
00:10:51,310 --> 00:10:52,905
Hey, you!

204
00:10:53,998 --> 00:10:59,908
At your age, you should know your place.

205
00:10:59,910 --> 00:11:02,806
You're just as old as I am.

206
00:11:02,808 --> 00:11:07,365
You think you can take advantage
of our sweet Sa Bin, don't you?

207
00:11:07,632 --> 00:11:10,272
- Let me go!
- You're unbelievably rude...

208
00:11:11,126 --> 00:11:12,126
I'm home...

209
00:11:13,724 --> 00:11:15,384
Mom!

210
00:11:15,932 --> 00:11:17,658
I swear, I...

211
00:11:19,118 --> 00:11:20,518
I can't believe this.

212
00:11:21,445 --> 00:11:24,733
You are never marrying him.

213
00:11:25,994 --> 00:11:26,994
Who are you?

214
00:11:27,192 --> 00:11:28,252
Why are you doing this?

215
00:11:28,658 --> 00:11:30,925
I'm Sa Bin's sister-in-law. Why?

216
00:11:31,372 --> 00:11:34,512
Your mom has the nerve
to marry into our family.

217
00:11:34,791 --> 00:11:37,218
You should talk some sense into her.

218
00:11:39,372 --> 00:11:40,565
Don't touch him.

219
00:11:40,885 --> 00:11:43,311
Whether I marry him is my choice.

220
00:11:43,465 --> 00:11:44,911
Stay out of it.

221
00:11:45,312 --> 00:11:46,312
Mom.

222
00:11:46,807 --> 00:11:48,400
You'd marry into a family like this?

223
00:11:48,641 --> 00:11:49,641
Right.

224
00:11:49,745 --> 00:11:52,298
Your husband abandoned you,
but you still have big ambitions.

225
00:11:52,532 --> 00:11:54,252
You've gone too far.

226
00:11:54,340 --> 00:11:56,164
- Don't insult my mother.
- Go inside.

227
00:11:56,166 --> 00:11:57,575
Then don't let her do that to you.

228
00:11:58,403 --> 00:12:01,145
- What's going on here?
- That's what I've been saying.

229
00:12:01,331 --> 00:12:03,085
I'll oppose this to the very end.

230
00:12:03,738 --> 00:12:05,705
Sa Bin can't just leave us.

231
00:12:05,984 --> 00:12:08,402
I cared for him, and my husband...

232
00:12:08,717 --> 00:12:11,133
has been like a father to Sa Bin.

233
00:12:11,308 --> 00:12:13,531
Do you know what it's like
to have a brother like a father?

234
00:12:13,965 --> 00:12:17,445
Because of your mother,
Sa Bin broke his brother's heart.

235
00:12:27,038 --> 00:12:29,484
They're grown adults
who made this decision carefully.

236
00:12:30,259 --> 00:12:32,105
So please don't come here again.

237
00:12:39,778 --> 00:12:42,258
I wouldn't come here
even if I were invited.

238
00:13:05,545 --> 00:13:07,225
I thought everyone had approved.

239
00:13:08,392 --> 00:13:09,804
After being treated like this,

240
00:13:10,405 --> 00:13:11,632
why would you still marry him?

241
00:13:12,738 --> 00:13:15,098
- I'll handle it.
- Don't marry him.

242
00:13:16,278 --> 00:13:17,791
I never truly supported this.

243
00:13:17,991 --> 00:13:19,963
I accepted it because you wanted it.

244
00:13:20,750 --> 00:13:21,750
But opposition like this?

245
00:13:22,771 --> 00:13:24,085
I never expected it.

246
00:13:27,011 --> 00:13:28,011
Mom.

247
00:13:29,107 --> 00:13:31,411
Okay. I understand your point.

248
00:13:32,492 --> 00:13:34,193
After seeing that, it would be odd...

249
00:13:35,054 --> 00:13:36,225
if you didn't object.

250
00:13:38,198 --> 00:13:39,198
Yeong Ju.

251
00:13:39,699 --> 00:13:42,398
- Can't we just...
- No.

252
00:13:45,692 --> 00:13:47,145
I don't want to stay here anymore.

253
00:13:48,365 --> 00:13:49,991
I'll start a new life with Sa Bin.

254
00:13:51,298 --> 00:13:54,851
We won't live in their house anyway.

255
00:13:55,544 --> 00:13:58,311
I just need to avoid seeing her often.

256
00:13:58,445 --> 00:14:01,058
She's his sister-in-law, not his mother.

257
00:14:03,164 --> 00:14:04,913
I thought about this for so long...

258
00:14:05,714 --> 00:14:07,410
before making such a big decision.

259
00:14:08,345 --> 00:14:09,758
I don't want to give up now.

260
00:14:10,771 --> 00:14:12,008
I'm going to...

261
00:14:12,809 --> 00:14:14,018
keep my promise to Sa Bin.

262
00:14:16,625 --> 00:14:19,438
- Mom.
- I'm sorry you had to see that.

263
00:14:20,585 --> 00:14:21,906
It breaks my heart,

264
00:14:22,960 --> 00:14:24,718
but I can't keep living this way.

265
00:14:26,132 --> 00:14:27,132
Seung Woo.

266
00:14:28,124 --> 00:14:29,124
I want to love...

267
00:14:30,011 --> 00:14:33,718
and be loved too.

268
00:14:35,478 --> 00:14:37,198
Before I die, just once,

269
00:14:40,011 --> 00:14:41,011
I want to live...

270
00:14:42,429 --> 00:14:43,838
the way everyone else does.

271
00:15:13,552 --> 00:15:15,465
So your family opposes this marriage?

272
00:15:15,778 --> 00:15:17,484
I won't let my mom
join a family that rejects her.

273
00:15:17,718 --> 00:15:18,718
Your family...

274
00:15:19,190 --> 00:15:20,824
has a higher standing than ours,

275
00:15:21,258 --> 00:15:22,274
and my mom's background...

276
00:15:22,755 --> 00:15:23,755
I know how it looks.

277
00:15:23,898 --> 00:15:25,094
Depending on how it's viewed,

278
00:15:25,415 --> 00:15:26,998
she may seem unsuitable.

279
00:15:27,424 --> 00:15:29,637
Please sit down so we can talk.

280
00:15:30,012 --> 00:15:31,450
I don't understand any of this.

281
00:15:31,452 --> 00:15:33,032
That sister-in-law of yours came by.

282
00:15:33,645 --> 00:15:34,810
She and my mom had a huge argument.

283
00:15:35,197 --> 00:15:36,390
I didn't know about that.

284
00:15:36,612 --> 00:15:38,724
- I'll handle it.
- That's what I came to stop.

285
00:15:39,732 --> 00:15:40,838
Don't try to fix this.

286
00:15:41,592 --> 00:15:42,992
End this relationship here.

287
00:15:43,485 --> 00:15:44,491
My mom...

288
00:15:45,499 --> 00:15:46,718
has suffered enough.

289
00:15:47,579 --> 00:15:50,129
Actually, more than anything,

290
00:15:51,450 --> 00:15:52,450
she's been lonely.

291
00:15:53,232 --> 00:15:57,425
She spent her whole life
caring for our grandparents and us...

292
00:15:59,858 --> 00:16:01,112
Anyway, please don't marry her.

293
00:16:01,492 --> 00:16:04,598
I don't want to see my mom cry again.

294
00:16:05,512 --> 00:16:08,185
- I won't make her cry.
- She's already cried.

295
00:16:08,925 --> 00:16:11,025
You should've handled this sooner.

296
00:16:11,605 --> 00:16:13,165
You shouldn't have let her get hit.

297
00:16:13,398 --> 00:16:15,630
You shouldn't have let her hear
that your family was against it!

298
00:16:16,225 --> 00:16:17,225
Am I wrong?

299
00:16:17,978 --> 00:16:19,191
Why are they against it?

300
00:16:19,399 --> 00:16:20,612
Did she hide that she had children?

301
00:16:21,072 --> 00:16:22,707
Did she claim she'd never been married?

302
00:16:23,432 --> 00:16:24,922
You knew everything when you proposed.

303
00:16:25,783 --> 00:16:26,783
Yes, that's true.

304
00:16:27,450 --> 00:16:29,537
I told my brother all that
from the beginning. But...

305
00:16:29,965 --> 00:16:31,707
I never thought this would happen.

306
00:16:32,102 --> 00:16:33,745
I'm so sorry.

307
00:16:34,985 --> 00:16:38,428
But how is Yeong Ju now?

308
00:16:39,496 --> 00:16:40,496
Don't do this.

309
00:16:41,305 --> 00:16:44,285
I can't support this anymore either.

310
00:16:46,758 --> 00:16:48,298
Seung Woo, wait a moment...

311
00:17:02,305 --> 00:17:04,172
Then why did you go?

312
00:17:04,525 --> 00:17:06,425
How could I not go?

313
00:17:06,964 --> 00:17:09,277
Would you really send Sa Bin
to a woman like that?

314
00:17:09,478 --> 00:17:13,171
You kept saying you wanted kids.
Have you given up on that?

315
00:17:14,205 --> 00:17:16,279
Even if you've given up on kids,

316
00:17:16,746 --> 00:17:19,111
at least they should be a good match.

317
00:17:20,872 --> 00:17:21,872
Here.

318
00:17:23,856 --> 00:17:24,856
Sun Kyung!

319
00:17:25,947 --> 00:17:27,104
You scared me.

320
00:17:27,800 --> 00:17:28,800
What?

321
00:17:28,985 --> 00:17:32,228
Did she run off to tell you already?
That I hit her?

322
00:17:33,643 --> 00:17:34,958
She hit me too.

323
00:17:35,278 --> 00:17:37,231
I got hit even worse.

324
00:17:37,445 --> 00:17:40,698
- Do you know how vicious she is?
- What's wrong with you?

325
00:17:41,192 --> 00:17:43,465
What am I supposed to do?

326
00:17:44,032 --> 00:17:45,513
Don't do this.

327
00:17:46,238 --> 00:17:48,278
She's not right for you.

328
00:17:49,519 --> 00:17:50,932
Sun Kyung!

329
00:17:54,767 --> 00:17:55,767
Come out.

330
00:17:57,260 --> 00:17:58,260
Come out.

331
00:18:03,792 --> 00:18:04,792
My head hurts.

332
00:18:10,638 --> 00:18:13,193
I barely got permission.

333
00:18:13,794 --> 00:18:17,111
But now her son says no.
He told me not to.

334
00:18:17,825 --> 00:18:19,270
Why are you doing this to me?

335
00:18:19,272 --> 00:18:20,871
Did I ask you to help me?

336
00:18:22,859 --> 00:18:25,278
I just asked you not to get in my way.

337
00:18:25,418 --> 00:18:26,418
Sa Bin.

338
00:18:26,810 --> 00:18:29,105
It's my first time. You know that.

339
00:18:31,832 --> 00:18:33,849
Since her marriage wasn't going well,

340
00:18:33,851 --> 00:18:36,518
do you know how relieved I felt inside?

341
00:18:37,992 --> 00:18:38,992
I thought, "What a relief!"

342
00:18:40,508 --> 00:18:41,978
"I'll treat her well."

343
00:18:42,095 --> 00:18:45,472
"I'll make her happier
than anyone else in this world."

344
00:18:46,779 --> 00:18:48,678
Just imagining it made me happy.

345
00:18:50,271 --> 00:18:52,971
Why can't you understand how I feel?

346
00:18:53,618 --> 00:18:56,691
Sun Kyung did all this for you.

347
00:18:58,685 --> 00:18:59,738
Please get her to apologize.

348
00:19:00,672 --> 00:19:02,465
What? What did you say?

349
00:19:02,865 --> 00:19:05,991
I want her to go apologize to Yeong Ju.

350
00:19:09,291 --> 00:19:10,778
Please, Joong Bin. I'm begging you.

351
00:19:13,525 --> 00:19:14,605
There you are, Uncle.

352
00:19:17,111 --> 00:19:18,658
See you later.

353
00:19:30,932 --> 00:19:32,382
Are you feeling refreshed
after spending time at the beach?

354
00:19:33,525 --> 00:19:34,525
Yes.

355
00:19:34,672 --> 00:19:35,672
Want some?

356
00:19:36,792 --> 00:19:38,088
Did you like it back then?

357
00:19:38,195 --> 00:19:39,978
Of course. It's my hometown.

358
00:19:40,465 --> 00:19:41,962
Though you were hardly ever home.

359
00:19:42,103 --> 00:19:43,218
Have you heard from Do Hee?

360
00:19:43,425 --> 00:19:45,025
She called a few times,
but I didn't answer.

361
00:19:46,112 --> 00:19:47,698
I'm sorry I disappointed you.

362
00:19:48,252 --> 00:19:50,245
I'll try to act more like your son.

363
00:19:51,125 --> 00:19:53,076
If you're still interested in the arts,

364
00:19:53,523 --> 00:19:55,892
consider taking over
the publishing company.

365
00:19:56,580 --> 00:19:57,651
Yes, thank you.

366
00:20:01,932 --> 00:20:02,932
Ji Hu.

367
00:20:03,215 --> 00:20:04,215
Yes.

368
00:20:04,403 --> 00:20:06,897
I know a child needs to learn a lesson
if he doesn't appreciate what he has,

369
00:20:07,011 --> 00:20:10,011
but hearing you say "Thank you"
every time hurts me too.

370
00:20:10,965 --> 00:20:12,252
Does it?

371
00:20:12,538 --> 00:20:14,504
That's not how I feel. You know that.

372
00:20:14,665 --> 00:20:15,665
Yes, I know.

373
00:20:48,005 --> 00:20:50,211
Your mom works part-time
at a clothing store.

374
00:20:50,752 --> 00:20:52,965
I stopped by to buy some clothes
and was so surprised.

375
00:20:53,772 --> 00:20:57,525
She asked me to keep it from you,
but I accidentally let it slip.

376
00:20:58,345 --> 00:21:01,515
Now that you know,
don't be too hard on her.

377
00:21:02,423 --> 00:21:03,423
Idiot.

378
00:21:05,643 --> 00:21:06,643
Idiot.

379
00:21:10,392 --> 00:21:12,572
You know the wrist tremors musicians get?

380
00:21:12,952 --> 00:21:14,798
She hasn't been able to teach
for a while because of it.

381
00:22:47,505 --> 00:22:48,505
Ji Ni.

382
00:22:50,694 --> 00:22:51,694
Ji Hu.

383
00:22:53,422 --> 00:22:54,570
What brings you here?

384
00:22:54,732 --> 00:22:55,840
What are you doing here?

385
00:22:56,205 --> 00:22:57,345
It's getting late.

386
00:22:58,558 --> 00:22:59,676
It's just...

387
00:23:00,397 --> 00:23:01,836
I was about to head home,

388
00:23:02,624 --> 00:23:04,605
but I had a lot on my mind.

389
00:23:06,732 --> 00:23:08,918
I heard you went to the beach.

390
00:23:11,378 --> 00:23:15,018
I went there to clear my head,
but I came back with even more on my mind.

391
00:23:16,278 --> 00:23:17,278
But...

392
00:23:18,232 --> 00:23:21,251
we said we wouldn't meet
like this anymore.

393
00:23:22,925 --> 00:23:23,958
I'll leave soon.

394
00:23:25,385 --> 00:23:27,305
But is something wrong?

395
00:23:28,265 --> 00:23:29,918
Is it about your mom?

396
00:23:34,392 --> 00:23:35,392
I...

397
00:23:36,185 --> 00:23:37,927
keep making things harder for my mom.

398
00:23:39,373 --> 00:23:40,824
It's killing me.

399
00:23:41,058 --> 00:23:43,952
You're probably thinking again,
"I shouldn't have been born."

400
00:23:45,058 --> 00:23:46,508
I try not to,

401
00:23:47,796 --> 00:23:50,095
but I keep getting lost in those thoughts.

402
00:23:51,689 --> 00:23:52,698
I feel the same way.

403
00:23:56,292 --> 00:23:59,551
I wonder why they abandoned me,
and I resent them,

404
00:24:00,019 --> 00:24:01,450
then I soon feel guilty.

405
00:24:02,851 --> 00:24:04,815
I think about how hard it must've been
for them because of me,

406
00:24:05,356 --> 00:24:06,845
then I think of the people
I'm grateful to.

407
00:24:09,152 --> 00:24:10,991
I guess I'm grateful they saved me.

408
00:24:14,505 --> 00:24:17,411
- Why are you laughing?
- Because now I know how Jung A feels.

409
00:24:19,111 --> 00:24:20,818
Sometimes when I say something,

410
00:24:21,232 --> 00:24:24,565
Jung A looks completely confused...

411
00:24:24,698 --> 00:24:26,518
because I'm saying things
only I understand.

412
00:24:27,585 --> 00:24:28,765
That's what I just did, right?

413
00:24:34,445 --> 00:24:35,445
I...

414
00:24:36,704 --> 00:24:38,218
was abandoned at birth.

415
00:24:39,725 --> 00:24:41,345
My adoptive parents raised me.

416
00:24:46,130 --> 00:24:48,897
- I had no idea.
- Of course you didn't.

417
00:24:50,252 --> 00:24:51,772
They're really good people.

418
00:24:52,738 --> 00:24:54,711
I try to repay their kindness every day.

419
00:24:57,818 --> 00:24:58,818
Do you remember...

420
00:24:59,360 --> 00:25:00,757
what you wrote beneath the painting...

421
00:25:01,185 --> 00:25:03,465
at the hotel when we first met?

422
00:25:04,185 --> 00:25:06,144
Flawed people come together...

423
00:25:06,565 --> 00:25:08,691
to make a whole family.

424
00:25:08,718 --> 00:25:10,991
Those words really resonated with me.

425
00:25:12,852 --> 00:25:14,310
Now that I think about it,

426
00:25:15,304 --> 00:25:19,191
I thought we'd be even more flawed,
since we all had our flaws.

427
00:25:20,351 --> 00:25:21,918
So that's what happened.

428
00:25:22,245 --> 00:25:24,765
I asked if you wrote it yourself.

429
00:25:25,571 --> 00:25:26,571
And then...

430
00:25:26,650 --> 00:25:29,952
you looked at me like some random stranger
and barely answered me.

431
00:25:30,220 --> 00:25:31,220
You don't remember?

432
00:25:31,389 --> 00:25:32,389
Me?

433
00:25:33,894 --> 00:25:36,165
- No way.
- I'm serious.

434
00:25:37,032 --> 00:25:38,592
You really hurt my feelings that day.

435
00:25:40,592 --> 00:25:41,592
I'm...

436
00:25:42,202 --> 00:25:44,762
pretty guarded around other people.

437
00:25:45,423 --> 00:25:46,423
I'm sorry.

438
00:25:46,735 --> 00:25:47,735
I understand.

439
00:25:49,225 --> 00:25:50,785
Thanks for not being shocked.

440
00:25:51,452 --> 00:25:52,498
You're the first person I've told.

441
00:25:52,891 --> 00:25:54,618
My parents don't know that I know.

442
00:25:57,625 --> 00:25:59,376
Until you decide to tell them,

443
00:26:00,444 --> 00:26:01,758
I'll keep it a secret.

444
00:26:04,412 --> 00:26:07,720
A blessed child, a less fortunate child.

445
00:26:08,441 --> 00:26:10,058
People are so quick
to divide us into categories.

446
00:26:28,992 --> 00:26:30,581
An off-season beach souvenir.

447
00:26:32,889 --> 00:26:35,225
It's pretty. Did you find it?

448
00:26:40,005 --> 00:26:41,005
Why?

449
00:26:42,055 --> 00:26:45,603
It's pretty, but there's nothing inside,
just like me.

450
00:26:50,532 --> 00:26:53,432
People think I was born into a good family
and have everything,

451
00:26:54,486 --> 00:26:55,945
but I'm actually empty inside.

452
00:26:58,172 --> 00:26:59,772
I'm going to try to fill that emptiness.

453
00:27:02,245 --> 00:27:03,758
Will you help me, Ji Ni?

454
00:27:50,020 --> 00:27:53,047
(Family Register)

455
00:27:53,049 --> 00:27:55,511
Don't get close to Sa Bin.
That's an order. It's my right.

456
00:27:55,513 --> 00:27:57,252
He's not Do Hee's fiancé anymore.
They broke up.

457
00:27:57,254 --> 00:27:58,956
Anyone can see how strange this is.

458
00:27:58,958 --> 00:28:00,383
Think carefully about what I said earlier.

459
00:28:00,385 --> 00:28:01,516
Ji Hu.

460
00:28:01,518 --> 00:28:03,071
Do Hee's going to get the wrong idea.

461
00:28:03,073 --> 00:28:04,192
Dad, please stop her.

462
00:28:04,194 --> 00:28:07,231
Even if I have to cut ties with my family,
I'll protect your mom.

463
00:28:07,233 --> 00:28:08,571
Choose. Sun Kyung or me?

464
00:28:08,573 --> 00:28:11,627
Come back after you convince her.
Otherwise, we're done.

465
00:28:11,629 --> 00:28:12,629
Sa Bin!

466
00:28:14,199 --> 00:28:16,199
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
